  "chapter": {
    "number": 24,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(25) A Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "To you, O Lord, have I lifted up my soul.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O my God, I have trusted in you: let me not be confounded, neither let my enemies laugh me to scorn.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For none of them that wait on you shall in any wise be ashamed: let them be ashamed that transgress without cause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Show me your ways, O Lord; and teach me your paths.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Lead me in your truth, and teach me: for you are God my Saviour: and I have waited on you all the day.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Remember your compassions, O Lord, and your mercies, for they are from everlasting.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Remember not the sins of my youth, nor my sins of ignorance: remember me according to your mercy, for your goodness' sake, O Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Good and upright is the Lord: therefore will he",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 43
          },
          {
            "text": "instruct sinners in the way.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The meek will he guide in judgment: the meek will he teach his ways.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "All the ways of the Lord are mercy and truth to them that seek his covenant and his testimonies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For your name's sake, O Lord, do you also be merciful to my sin; for it is great.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who is the man that fears the Lord? he shall instruct him in the way which he has chosen.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "His soul shall dwell in prosperity; and his seed shall inherit the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord is the strength of them that fear him; and his covenant is to manifest",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 44
          },
          {
            "text": "truth to them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My eyes are continually to the Lord; for he shall draw my feet out of the snare.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Look upon me, and have mercy upon me; for I am an only child and poor.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The afflictions of my heart have been multiplied; deliver me from my distresses.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Look upon my affliction and my trouble; and forgive all my sins.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Look upon my enemies; for they have been multiplied; and they have hated me with unjust hatred.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Keep my soul, and deliver me: let me not be ashamed; for I have hoped in you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The harmless and upright joined themselves to me: for I waited for you, O Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Deliver Israel, O God, out of all his afflictions.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 43,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "sc. as a law-giver",
